=== layout: one-panel

# Multiplication rules

@body

- *Independent events*: P(A and B) = P(A) &times; P(B)
- *General rule*: P(A and B) = P(A) &times; P(B|A)
- Equivalently: P(B) &times; P(A|B)
- Hear "and"? Think multiplication - then check independence.

=== layout: one-panel

# Addition rules

@body

- *Mutually exclusive events*: P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B)
- *General rule*: P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A and B)
- Hear "or"? Think addition - then check overlap.

=== layout: one-panel

# Practice: a puppy's genotype

@body

Two *BbCc* dogs are crossed.

- B: black coat; b: yellow coat
- C: straight fur; c: curly fur
- The genes assort independently and are not sex linked.

*What fraction of puppies will be BbCc?*

- First find P(Bb).
- Then find P(Cc).

@notes

P(Bb) = 1/2 and P(Cc) = 1/2, so P(BbCc) = 1/4.

