=== layout: one-panel

# More Practice

@body

- In dogs, black coat color (_B_) is dominant to yellow coat color (_b_), and straight fur (_C_) is dominant to curly fur (_c_). The coat color gene and the fur texture gene are on different chromosomes, so they assort independently, and are not sex linked.
- *In a cross between two* *_BbCc_* *parents, predict the fraction of offspring with black coat color and straight fur.*

=== layout: one-panel

# Black coat and straight fur

@body

- P(black) = P(BB or Bb) = 3/4
- P(straight) = P(CC or Cc) = 3/4
- Independent loci: multiply the phenotype probabilities.

*P(black and straight) = (3/4) &times; (3/4) = 9/16*

Expected fraction does not guarantee an exact count in a small litter.

=== layout: one-panel

# Key ideas to keep

@body

- AND: multiply; check independence.
- OR: add; subtract overlap when needed.
- A genotype and its dominant phenotype have different probabilities.

